  year         = {2026},
  howpublished = {Cryptology ePrint Archive, Paper 2026/013},
  note         = {\url{https://eprint.iacr.org/2026/013}. Short replicated
                  secret sharing (RSS): the joint signing key is a sum of
                  many \emph{short} per-subset secrets, so its $\ell_\infty$
                  norm stays inside the ML-DSA $S_\eta$-class admissibility
                  bound instead of growing with the number of parties. This
                  is the published escape from the naive-additive-$S_\eta$
                  wall and makes dealerless threshold ML-DSA \emph{keygen}
                  reachable; the group key signs under the stock FIPS-204
                  verifier.}
}

